End-to-End Project Summary: Snowflake Cost & Performance Governance Platform
1. USE CASE
This project is a Snowflake FinOps / Cost Governance and Performance Monitoring platform built entirely on Snowflake-native capabilities. It serves two purposes:

E-Commerce Analytics Pipeline (Medallion Architecture) — ingesting, cleansing, and modeling Brazilian e-commerce data through Bronze > Silver > Gold layers using Dynamic Tables.
Snowflake Account Cost & Performance Dashboard — a Streamlit app that queries Snowflake's own system views (ACCOUNT_USAGE, ORGANIZATION_USAGE, INFORMATION_SCHEMA) to provide real-time FinOps governance.
2. DATA ARCHITECTURE (Medallion / Lakehouse)
Database: ECOMMERCE_DEV

Schema	Purpose
BRONZE_LAYER	Raw tables (*_RAW) loaded via Snowpipe from external stage
STAGING_SCHEMA	Streams for CDC tracking
SILVER_LAYER	Cleansed, typed, deduplicated Dynamic Tables
GOLD_LAYER	Business-level aggregations (DIM_, FACT_, analytics marts)
DATA_QUALITY	DMF result views, expectations, score cards, reconciliation
MONITORING	Operational health views (DT refresh, tasks, queries, credits)
COST_ANALYTICS	FinOps governance views consumed by the Streamlit dashboard
SCHEMACHANGE	Migration history tracking
Entities: Customers, Orders, Order Items, Payments, Reviews, Products, Sellers, Geolocation

3. KEY SNOWFLAKE FEATURES USED
Feature	How It's Used
Dynamic Tables (TARGET_LAG 1h)	All Silver and Gold transformations — zero-maintenance incremental refresh
Streams + Tasks	CDC pipeline from Bronze to Silver
Snowpipe	Auto-ingest from external stage into Bronze
Cortex TRANSLATE	Portuguese review comments translated to English in Gold layer
Privacy Tags	PRIVACY_LEVEL, SEMANTIC_CATEGORY on PII columns
DMFs (Data Metric Functions)	Automated data quality checks with expectations
Schemachange	Version-controlled migrations (V*.sql = versioned, R*.sql = repeatable)
SPCS (Container Runtime)	Streamlit app runs on SYSTEM_COMPUTE_POOL_CPU
ACCOUNT_USAGE views	Foundation for all cost/perf analytics
4. THE STREAMLIT APPLICATION
Location: ECOMMERCE_DEV.COST_ANALYTICS.COST_ANALYTICS_DASHBOARD
Runtime: SPCS (Container Pool)
16 Tabs:

#	Tab	What It Shows
1	Overview	7-day spend, monthly projection, MTD USD, weekly/monthly trends
2	Warehouses	Daily credit usage, utilization %, MoM change, top resources
3	Users	Per-user cost attribution, expensive query patterns
4	Serverless	Task credits, Snowpipe, clustering, materialized views, search optimization
5	Storage	Daily storage growth and trends
6	Query Performance	Slow queries, queue times, full table scans, spilling
7	Containers	SPCS compute pool costs, data transfer
8	Simulator	What-if warehouse sizing (user inputs, calculates projected savings)
9	Efficiency Score	Waste score per warehouse and per user
10	Budget Burn-Down	Budget vs actual spend, burn rate tracking
11	Remediation Console	Actionable ALTER WAREHOUSE / SUSPEND commands with copy-to-clipboard
12	Cost Velocity	Day-over-day cost acceleration/deceleration
13	Anomalies	Statistical outlier detection on daily spend
14	Anti-Patterns	Duplicate queries, failed queries
15	Concurrency & Sizing	Peak hour analysis, concurrency, sizing recommendations
16	Identity Governance	Inactive users, login failure patterns
Key Streamlit features: Role-based access tiers (ADMIN/ENGINEER/VIEWER), Slack/Teams webhook alerting, cached queries (TTL 600s), dynamic chart rendering, custom CSS design system.

